1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,065
One soldier carries thirty-two kilos.

2
00:00:03,065 --> 00:00:05,000
The other carries thirty.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,103
Same war, same job, two completely different answers.

4
00:00:09,103 --> 00:00:15,374
This is American gear against Chinese gear, item by item, starting at the muzzle.

5
00:00:16,624 --> 00:00:22,095
Start with the rifle, because everything else on the belt exists to feed it.

6
00:00:22,095 --> 00:00:25,838
America's M7 fires a brand new 6.8 millimetre round,

7
00:00:25,838 --> 00:00:29,941
designed to punch through modern body armour at distance.

8
00:00:29,941 --> 00:00:35,771
China's QBZ nineteen-one keeps the proven 5.8 millimetre cartridge, in a lighter,

9
00:00:35,771 --> 00:00:37,139
more compact rifle.

10
00:00:37,939 --> 00:00:40,323
The trade is energy against weight.

11
00:00:40,323 --> 00:00:44,341
The American round carries roughly twice the muzzle energy,

12
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:47,678
and costs about twice the mass in every magazine.

13
00:00:47,678 --> 00:00:52,173
For the man carrying it, that is the whole argument in one number.

14
00:00:52,973 --> 00:00:57,662
Camouflage is a design argument about where you expect to fight.

15
00:00:57,662 --> 00:01:04,037
The US operational camouflage pattern blends tan and green for a wide range of terrain.

16
00:01:04,037 --> 00:01:10,632
China's star-sky pattern goes digital, tuned for its own coastlines, highlands and cities.

17
00:01:11,432 --> 00:01:14,177
Both armies have moved to the high-cut helmet.

18
00:01:14,177 --> 00:01:18,115
The trade is the same on both sides: less coverage around the ear,

19
00:01:18,115 --> 00:01:22,949
so a headset and a night vision mount can sit against the skull without pinching.

20
00:01:23,749 --> 00:01:28,886
Body armour has quietly become the heaviest thing a soldier wears.

21
00:01:28,886 --> 00:01:32,778
Both systems carry two hard plates front and back,

22
00:01:32,778 --> 00:01:39,004
then hang everything else from the same shell: magazines, radio, water, medical.

23
00:01:39,804 --> 00:01:41,977
Neither vest is a suit of armour.

24
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:46,321
Both leave the shoulders, the sides and the groin largely exposed,

25
00:01:46,321 --> 00:01:50,403
and both rely on add-on panels when the mission asks for them.

26
00:01:50,403 --> 00:01:52,970
Coverage is a decision, not a constant.

27
00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:57,610
Dual-tube night vision used to be an American privilege.

28
00:01:57,610 --> 00:02:01,998
It is now standard issue in China's modernised brigades as well.

29
00:02:01,998 --> 00:02:05,837
Twenty years ago this scene looked completely different;

30
00:02:05,837 --> 00:02:08,306
today the goggles are close cousins.

31
00:02:09,106 --> 00:02:11,543
The rifle is only half the system.

32
00:02:11,543 --> 00:02:17,852
America issues a variable optic that goes from one power for a doorway to eight for four

33
00:02:17,852 --> 00:02:18,927
hundred metres.

34
00:02:18,927 --> 00:02:25,522
China's answer is a simpler fixed three power prism: lighter, cheaper, and fast to train on.

35
00:02:26,322 --> 00:02:31,955
Listen closely to a modern infantry squad and you hear two networks: the local net that

36
00:02:31,955 --> 00:02:36,228
keeps a fire team together, and the long one that reaches command.

37
00:02:36,228 --> 00:02:40,695
Both armies are pushing the second down to smaller and smaller units.

38
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:43,428
Every fire team needs a weapon it can lean on.

39
00:02:43,428 --> 00:02:47,166
America replaced its decades-old squad automatic with a belt-fed light machine gun in the

40
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:47,671
new calibre.

41
00:02:47,671 --> 00:02:49,645
China fielded its own lightweight belt-fed gun,

42
00:02:49,645 --> 00:02:51,745
and the two numbers land in almost the same place.

43
00:02:53,295 --> 00:02:57,045
For years the sidearm was a status symbol for officers and machine gunners.

44
00:02:57,045 --> 00:02:59,845
Both armies now push a full-size pistol into more hands,

45
00:02:59,845 --> 00:03:02,545
mostly as the last option when a primary weapon fails.

46
00:03:04,095 --> 00:03:06,014
Under every second rifle sits a small cannon.

47
00:03:06,014 --> 00:03:09,893
The American forty millimetre and the Chinese thirty-five are used for the same three jobs:

48
00:03:09,893 --> 00:03:13,345
breaking a position, laying smoke, and marking a target for someone further away.

49
00:03:14,895 --> 00:03:17,230
A soldier burns more calories than any ration provides,

50
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:20,160
which is why field food is designed around density rather than taste.

51
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:22,664
The Chinese self-heating pouch is the smaller, faster meal.

52
00:03:22,664 --> 00:03:26,145
The American ration is the bigger, heavier one, with more snacks packed around it.

53
00:03:27,695 --> 00:03:30,186
Water is the one item nobody argues about.

54
00:03:30,186 --> 00:03:33,150
Three litres on the body, refilled at every pause,

55
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:36,945
and a full bladder adds more weight than the rifle's ammunition.

56
00:03:38,495 --> 00:03:43,303
Both armies learned the same lesson in the last twenty years: the individual soldier has to

57
00:03:43,303 --> 00:03:44,466
stop his own bleeding.

58
00:03:44,466 --> 00:03:48,745
Tourniquets moved from the medics bag onto the body, where a hand can reach them.

59
00:03:50,295 --> 00:03:52,394
Ten years ago this chapter would not exist.

60
00:03:52,394 --> 00:03:56,445
Today the smallest aircraft in the inventory is carried by the infantryman himself,

61
00:03:56,445 --> 00:04:00,545
launched by hand, and used to look over the next wall before anyone walks around it.

62
00:04:02,095 --> 00:04:03,619
Here is the honest ending.

63
00:04:03,619 --> 00:04:05,905
After eighteen chapters of differences,

64
00:04:05,905 --> 00:04:09,598
the two soldiers arrive within a couple of kilos of each other.

65
00:04:09,598 --> 00:04:14,345
Thirty kilos is not a design choice; it is what a human being can still fight in.

66
00:04:15,895 --> 00:04:17,840
Two nations, two doctrines, one conclusion.

67
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,689
The American soldier is built to see further and call for more.

68
00:04:20,689 --> 00:04:23,628
The Chinese soldier is built to move with mass and stay supplied.

69
00:04:23,628 --> 00:04:26,568
Different ideas, but the same thirty kilos on the same shoulders.

70
00:04:26,568 --> 00:04:29,145
If you want the next comparison, tell me in the comments.

